mod-animus-movement.patch -- the movement-smooth work for the realm module: A1-A5, A7, A9, B and D (forge commits
e0aac3412..2f7f4d155). C (the jitter prices), A6, A8 (the dungeon advance; the realm has no wing routes) and A10 are
sim-only. A snapshot: the forge's MoveBlock has moved on with C and A8, so a later resync starts from a diverged file.

Apply in modules/mod-animus with `patch -p1`, after mod-animus-amdl8.patch (either order gives the same tree; on
the bare module it applies with offsets). Realm-specific (stock AzerothCore has no MoveSpline::ReaimFacing and no
PressesFirst): Encoding::ReaimRun turns only the unit, for this decision's press, and MoveBlock's Steer relaunches
a run whose launch facing is more than Animus.Curriculum.Options.ShownFacingRelaunchDeg (default 20) off where the
seat looks -- always, not only with a client watching; Block::BeforePress runs before BeforeApply, and the press
after Steer; there is no per-tick hook (FaceTargetBetween, ShowTurn) -- CompanionParty::TurnShown shows turns,
seeded from the run's launch facing; a refreshed held bearing skips SeatMemory::Press. Animus.MoveRevision (default
0, logged once at load) selects the move block's revision 1 (D) for models trained with AnimusForge.MoveRevision 1;
its features read Animus.Curriculum.Options.JitterDecayMs (2500), the forge's decay. At revision 0 the observations
are unchanged (only the held-bearing mask).

--- a/animus-lib/src/runtime/Scenario/Curriculum/Blocks/CoreBlock.cpp
+++ b/animus-lib/src/runtime/Scenario/Curriculum/Blocks/CoreBlock.cpp
@@ -451,8 +451,15 @@
